cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FITA — Flexible Image Transfer Alpha"
message: "If you use this software or the FITA convention, please cite it."
type: software
abstract: >-
  FITA is a FITS convention for multi-layer astronomical images that lets a
  user balance data so as to re-naturalise sliced and measured phenomena lying
  beyond the reach of human senses, while maintaining the scientific integrity
  of the measurements. Calibrated flux is held in FLUX_* extensions and
  display transparency in paired ALPHA_* extensions, so re-selecting a display
  range changes only what the eye sees and never the measured flux, verified
  bit-for-bit. It adds per-layer blend modes, non-destructive adjustment
  layers, stereo depth encoding physical ISM penetration, and IVOA ObsCore
  v1.2 provenance, while remaining a valid FITS multi-extension file readable
  by any FITS reader. Designed for multi-wavelength astronomy and the
  integration of multispectral measurements into physical models and
  astrophysical inference, FITA is intended to be multi-wavelength and
  multidisciplinary, and is at the heart of the MWVO (Multi-Wave Virtual
  Observatory).
